  "tibetan_transliteration": "\u0f62\u0f72\u0f42\u0f66\u0f0b\u0f50\u0f72\u0f42\u0f66\u0f0b\u0f60\u0f42\u0fb2\u0f7a\u0f63\u0f0b\u0f54\u0f60\u0f72\u0f0b\u0f51\u0f7c\u0f53\u0f0b\u0f56\u0f66\u0fa1\u0f74\u0f66",
  "comments": "This work is a concise guide to Dharmottara's Ny\u0101yabindu\u1e6d\u012bk\u0101 (ID:3779), and not to the Pram\u0101\u1e47avini\u015bcaya, as the [S635TW6P] title (tshad ma rnam nges kyi bsdus don) suggests. The colophons identifies it as an \"explanation of the five 'bam po'.\" \"The Five bam po\" is a nickname for the Ny\u0101yabindu\u1e6d\u012bk\u0101 based on its length as reported in the lHan dkar catalogue ([WAHGRFDB]: 336).\r\nSee [GHC9CLWS] for an introduction.\r\n\r\nThis work probably corresponds to the \"bsdus don\" listed by several Tibetan scholars (see <<Kano 2016 [BAQ9MH4T]>>: 205). A \"rnam bshad\" is also listed, which is not extant (ID: 6083).\r\n\r\nThe author cites the Pram\u0101\u1e47asamuccaya (ID:3770), the Pram\u0101\u1e47av\u0101rttika (ID:3772), the Pram\u0101\u1e47avini\u015bcaya (ID:3774) and Pram\u0101\u1e47avini\u015bcaya\u1e6d\u012bk\u0101 (ID:5594). He further refers four times to the views of other scholars without giving their name.",
  "alternative_names_legacy": "tshad ma rnam nges kyi bsdus don (sic)\r\nmtshan nyid kyi chos\r\nbam po lnga pa'i bshad pa\r\nrigs thigs 'grel don bsdus\r\nrigs thigs 'grel pa dang bcas pa'i bsdus don",
